<section>
  <h2>GPS coordinates: where the photo was taken</h2>
  <p>Some photos remember the street, not just the city.</p>
  <p>
    When location permission is on, a phone can write latitude, longitude and even altitude into the EXIF
    GPS block. Shared as-is, that photo metadata can reveal a home address, a workplace or a child's
    school. To remove that trail, this tool deletes the whole EXIF segment rather than editing single
    fields, so the GPS metadata is removed together with the rest of the block. The picture itself does
    not move a pixel.
  </p>
</section>
